---

## Lore

The pygmies call themselves the Jungle People: a small people of the Congo,
most standing four to four and a half feet tall, who know its jungles and the
ways of hunting and tracking better than anyone. Most tribes are nomadic
within the Congo, from a few dozen to over a thousand strong, led by a king,
queen and council of elders with a shaman rather than a medicine man. Some
two million live there.

They are wary of all outsiders, above all large people, D-bees and
monsters, and hate the supernatural as evil spirits to be slain or driven
out. Their truest allies are the small furred tree people, and they revere
the timid agogwe as sacred jungle spirits, the first men born of the Great
Tree of Life.

The hunters are among the most skilled hunters and trackers on the
continent: smart, courageous, and versed in every secret of the jungle.

## GM Notes

Pygmy legend tells of the Ancient Father, a Millennium Tree said to be the
first Tree of Life, whose low branches cover an area two miles across
somewhere in the Congo. Its location is a secret kept by pygmy priests,
medicine men and chiefs, who have died under torture rather than reveal it;
the pygmies who worship it have a will that no magic, psionics, drug or mind
control can break on that subject. A hunter may carry one or two charms or
talismans made by a pygmy shaman.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'pygmy-hunter');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'pygmy-hunter';

